# Architecture workflow

Before major changes:

1. Read `docs/architecture/README.md` and linked docs
2. Identify affected services: frontend, backend, runner, trame-viewer, ai
3. Follow existing patterns (REST via BFF, internal runner HTTP, postMessage bridge, AI XML contract in `backend/services/ccs/prompt.py`)
4. Reuse components; avoid duplicate job/volume paths or second viewers
5. Explain architectural impact in PRs or chat when non-obvious
6. Update `docs/architecture/` and service READMEs if behavior or boundaries change

Prefer: modular services, clear boundaries, low coupling, shared `jobs_data` volume as single filesystem truth for a job.

## Data flow (summary)

Upload ZIP → simulation service extracts to `/jobs/<id>/case/` → runner runs solver in container → logs/VTK on volume → Trame reads VTK → UI embeds viewer and optional AI context.

Do not bypass MongoDB for job metadata or mount ad-hoc host paths into solver containers (macOS bind-mount issues); use the named volume pattern in Compose.
